            0.201
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Unless stated otherwise, use the approximation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 2 2 } { 7 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for π."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.203,
            0.746,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. The perimeter of a circle is 44 cm. What is its radius?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.227,
            0.884,
            0.268
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Calculate, correct to 3 significant figures, the circumference of a circle with: (i) radius 7 cm (ii) radius 10 cm (iii) radius 12 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.27,
            0.885,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. Calculate the length of the arc of a circle if: (i) the radius is 3.5 cm and the angle at the centre is 60°, and (ii) the radius is 6.3 m and the angle at the centre is 120°."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.33,
            0.884,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Find the perimeter of a sector (i.e., the curved portion as well as the two straight portions) of a circle of radius 14 cm and sector angle "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "7 5 ^ { \\circ }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.373,
            0.886,
            0.436
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Find the perimeters of the following shapes (taking the arcs to be quarter or half or three-quarters of a circle, as appropriate) (Fig. 6.14i to 6.14ix):"
